From 6bcee1a5028f55f3e19cd91a90bedadb38c395dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:04:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/40] Fix forwarding of a global load past a call that
 overwrites the register

The peephole optimiser replaces reads of a zero page register by reads
of the global it was loaded from or stored to (LDA abs; STA zp and
STA zp; STA abs), walking forward from the store with
CheckSingleUseGlobalLoad and rewriting with PatchSingleUseGlobalLoad.
At a JSR the check continues when the callee is known not to store to
globals and does not use the register as a parameter or temporary. It
never asked whether the call changes the register: the branch that
tests ChangesZeroPage(reg) comes after the JSR branch and is not reached
for a call. PatchSingleUseGlobalLoad has no notion of calls at all.

With the register in ACCU, where every call leaves its result, the walk
went past the call and the read of the result's low byte behind it was
rewritten into a read of the global:

	char t[2]; unsigned r = 0;
	...
	t[0] = arr[k + 1];
	return r + t[0] + use(t);

compiled to r + t[0] + t[0] plus the high byte of use()'s result at
every native optimisation level above -O0. The byte had passed through
ACCU on its way into t[0], r + t[0] was added up before the call, and
liveness keeps ACCU alive across a call.

Both walks now end at a call for which ChangesZeroPage(reg) holds, the
way they end at a store to the register: the reads in front of the call
are still forwarded, the ones behind it are left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
index 08a31a7..7b070bb 100644
--- a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -34485,6 +34485,21 @@ bool NativeCodeBasicBlock::CheckSingleUseGlobalLoad(const NativeCodeBasicBlock*
 				}
 				else
 					return false;
+
+				// The call does not disturb the global, but it may overwrite the
+				// zero page register itself (its result in ACCU, its scratch in
+				// WORK, ADDR and the caller saved temporaries).  The value in reg
+				// ends here, as it does at a store: a read of reg behind the call
+				// sees the value the call left there and must not be patched.
+				if (ins.ChangesZeroPage(reg))
+				{
+					if (mTrueJump && !mTrueJump->CheckPatchFailReg(block, reg))
+						return false;
+					if (mFalseJump && !mFalseJump->CheckPatchFailReg(block, reg))
+						return false;
+
+					return true;
+				}
 			}
 			else if (ains.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_X && ins.ChangesXReg())
 				return false;
@@ -34582,6 +34597,8 @@ bool NativeCodeBasicBlock::PatchSingleUseGlobalLoad(const NativeCodeBasicBlock*
 				else
 					return changed;
 			}
+			else if (ins.mType == ASMIT_JSR && ins.ChangesZeroPage(reg))
+				return changed;
 
 			if (ains.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_X)
 				ins.mLive |= LIVE_CPU_REG_X;
